+// Senua AI patch, in design (off unless MUJOCO_NOSLIP_NORMAL=1), its second version: noslip's pass also moves each
+// elliptic contact's normal force, as MuJoCo's own PGS moves an elliptic contact: first a ray update, the contact's
+// whole force scaled along itself (so it stays in the cone), then the friction with the normal fixed. In the ray update
+// the normal row keeps its regularization and the friction rows go without theirs, as noslip treats them. Noslip
+// re-solves the friction with every normal force held as the main solver left it; a free cube pushed near its limit
+// then rocks on its front edge, and offset stacks keep turning (runs 093, 096). Pyramidal contacts are unchanged.
+static int noslipNormalOn(void) {
+  const char* s = getenv("MUJOCO_NOSLIP_NORMAL");
+  return s && s[0] == '1' && s[1] == 0;
+}
+
